Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["STAGE 2: \nBoyer-Lindquist coordinates + class-III \
rotated Kinnersley tetrad",
 FontSize->22]], "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.996119382550145*^9, 3.996119412220377*^9}, {
   3.9961199988096294`*^9, 3.9961200086794276`*^9}, 
   3.996120052082369*^9},ExpressionUUID->"e00e82a0-f7c4-41bb-92f0-\
acf22cd39af6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Under a tetrad transformation, the coordinate basis components of the \
metric do not change, hence neither do the components of the curvature \
tensors thus constructed. However, the NP scalars (Ricci, Weyl, spin \
coefficients) will transform under the rotation. \n\nNo need to re-evaluate \
the curvature tensors. \nThe choice of class-III rotation parameters is, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"A", " ", "="}], " ", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Theta]", "=", "0"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->"TraditionalForm",ExpressionUUID->
  "600ae6f2-9d45-4128-a9d8-9133ae8d2544"],
 ". \n\nSo first rotate the tetrad in abstract form, then apply the rotation \
parameters. Finally evaluate the NP scalars. \[LineSeparator]Workflow \
example:\nlVec[a]/.rotation3rules/.paramChoice (with older tetrad components) \
- stored as rotated vector - lVecR[a]?\nDo the rest with these?"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9961249559013925`*^9, 3.99612514862122*^9}, {
  3.996125181124439*^9, 
  3.996125327657158*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b1e2e784-5f4e-4cea-b259-\
1855a2b9dd72"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

